From 7d56994140acefa81cd5f6aa73a663da14ed21c4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 00:31:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(inventory): translate Bedrock loom inventories in core

Use the standard Java loom screen and advertised banner-pattern tag order
so ordinary Java clients can craft banners through ViaProxy. Preserve
native banner metadata and layers when constructing the result and map
its colors and patterns to Java item components. Pattern materials remain
in the loom. Quick-moving results waits for each authoritative response.

Bedrock 1.26.51.1 build 51061372, protocol 2193, native captures establish
physical slots 9/10/11/50, named containers 41/42/43/44, CraftLoom plus
CraftResults actions, consumption of the banner and dye, and placement of
CreatedOutput slot 50 into the cursor. Native hh and cre crafts succeed.
Close returns inputs and the cursor before sending ContainerClose using
the shared acknowledged input-container lifecycle.
